# Chain is authority

`lib/launchpad/launch-solver.ts` is a **preview**. The Factory / EOL Token decide whether a launch is valid.

- UI **10%** treasury figure is the ASK (sizes the raise, blocks bad setups in the wizard).
- On-chain **8%** is the accept floor after USDC→SOL slippage. A launch can land between 8% and 10%.
- Combined backing **18%** is also on-chain. Do not fold 10% and 8% into one constant.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
const TREAS_FLOOR = 0.08; // used in both UI and "keep aligned with chain"

// ✅ GOOD
const TREASURY_ASK = 0.10;      // UI / solver
const TREASURY_ACCEPT = 0.08;   // document chain-only; do not drive the wizard with it
const COMBINED_BACKING_MIN = 0.18;
```

Wallet address is identity. Do not add a login or user table for launch.
